-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ט/5 (29.5.2019): רענון הנחיות בנושא מינוי מנהלים בחטיבה העליונה
-- How an owner of an upper division appoints its principal: the threshold
-- conditions of the Director-General's circular, the desirable skills,
-- the tender and its committee with the Ministry's two representatives,
-- the candidate file, the employment approval, and the Ministry's say.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר תשע"ט/5 מינוי מנהלים בחטיבה העליונה`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 The letterhead, date, reference, addressee, subject line and the heading "מבוא"; no rule.

-- akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18 akn:preamble/p20 akn:preamble/p21 akn:preamble/p22 akn:preamble/p23 akn:preamble/p24 akn:preamble/p25 The introduction: the Ministry's standing as employer and regulator, and the sources of its power to set principals' conditions (the Supervision of Schools Law 1969 sections 9 and 28, the State Education (Recognised Institutions) Regulations 1953, the Director-General's circular, the owner's licence undertaking); the operative rules they ground follow.

-- akn:preamble/p19 akn:preamble/p29 akn:art_4/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p14 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p28 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p31 The page's running header "משרד החינוך", printed in the text at each page break; no rule.

@desc An owner of an upper division, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `owner` HAS
    `owns an upper division (10-12 or 9-12)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supervised and budgeted by the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `licensed under the Supervision of Schools Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owns a six-year school` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `appointment action` IS ONE OF
    `appoint the candidate as principal`
    `check the candidate against the thresholds`
    `prepare the candidate file`
    `have the whole committee check the candidate file before the interview`
    `employ an education worker without the employment approval`
    `complete the principal training programme`

-- akn:preamble/p28 The heading "אוכלוסיית היעד"; no rule.

-- ¶30: the circular is addressed to the owners of upper divisions,
-- supervised and budgeted by the Ministry and licensed under the
-- Supervision of Schools Law.
@ref akn:preamble/p30
GIVEN o IS AN `owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular applies to` o IF
        o's `owns an upper division (10-12 or 9-12)`
    AND o's `supervised and budgeted by the Ministry`
    AND o's `licensed under the Supervision of Schools Law`

§§ `תנאי הסף למנהל בית ספר על יסודי`

-- akn:preamble/p31 akn:preamble/p34 Headings ("threshold conditions", "for a post-primary principal's post"); no rule.

@desc A candidate for principal of a post-primary school, as the threshold conditions ask.
DECLARE `candidate` HAS
    `years of actual teaching in grades 1-12 in Israel` IS A NUMBER @desc at a scope that earns teaching seniority; lecturing or tutoring at a university or college, PERACH coordination and the like do not count
    `full school years of actual teaching` IS A NUMBER
    `years of proven management` IS A NUMBER @desc full-time, with training, guiding or teaching of employees, proven by the workplace's HR officer
    `managed in the education system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `team size managed` IS A NUMBER
    `recognised master's degree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Israeli, or foreign with equivalence from the foreign-degrees evaluation department
    `post-primary pedagogical qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a certified or senior-certified teacher's certificate, a teaching certificate, a permanent teaching licence or licence to teach, or a university teaching certificate, for post-primary
    `principal training` IS A `principal training`
    `serving principal for 3 consecutive years with 3 approved years and no negative opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `former principal 4 of the last 10 years with 4 approved years and no negative opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `found unsuitable by a Ministry representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `found fit by the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `principal training` IS ONE OF
    `the Avney Rosha programme completed or eligible`
    `the Avney Rosha programme begun in July of the year before the posts are published` HAS
        `the tender closes before the programme ends` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an earlier Ministry programme for principals completed`
    `the 5769 pilot master's in school leadership`
    `a master's in education administration` HAS
        `begun by 5771 at the latest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `none`

-- Condition 1: five years of actual teaching in grades 1-12 in Israel.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has five years' teaching` c IF
    c's `years of actual teaching in grades 1-12 in Israel` AT LEAST 5

-- Condition 1's note: three full school years' teaching instead, with five
-- years' proven full-time management "in the education system or in a
-- system in which he managed a team of no fewer than 30". The reading
-- adopted (F-2018-19_tashat_05-a): the 30 qualifies only the other system.
-- akn:art_1/p2 The heading "הערה"; no rule.

@ref akn:art_1/p3
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the management alternative` c IF
        c's `full school years of actual teaching` AT LEAST 3
    AND c's `years of proven management` AT LEAST 5
    AND (c's `managed in the education system` OR c's `team size managed` AT LEAST 30)

@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p3
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the teaching condition` c IF
    `has five years' teaching` c OR `meets the management alternative` c

-- Condition 2: a recognised master's degree; in a religious school a Torah
-- education is desirable, not required.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the academic condition` c IF
    c's `recognised master's degree`

-- Condition 3: the post-primary pedagogical qualification.
@ref akn:art_3
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the pedagogical condition` c IF
    c's `post-primary pedagogical qualification`

-- Condition 4 and its alternatives 4.1-4.3. One who began Avney Rosha in
-- July of the year before counts, for tenders closing before the programme
-- ends (¶3, ¶5). A master's in education administration begun from 5772
-- on is no alternative (¶6; 4.3: begun by 5771 at the latest).
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4/p3 akn:art_4/p5 akn:art_4/p6 akn:art_4/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-3
GIVEN t IS A `principal training`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the training qualifies` t IF
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the Avney Rosha programme completed or eligible` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Avney Rosha programme begun in July of the year before the posts are published` closes THEN closes
    WHEN `an earlier Ministry programme for principals completed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the 5769 pilot master's in school leadership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a master's in education administration` early THEN early
    WHEN `none` THEN FALSE

-- 4.3: "education administration" names every master's programme in the
-- field, whatever an institution calls it; the list of each institution's
-- name for it, in the printed order.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p12 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p13 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p14 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p15 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p16 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p17 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p18 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p19 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p20 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p21
`the programmes that are education administration` MEANS
    LIST
        `education administration programme` "אוניברסיטת בן-גוריון" "מינהל, חברה ומדיניות החינוך",
        `education administration programme` "אוניברסיטת בר-אילן" "מינהל החינוך",
        `education administration programme` "אוניברסיטת חיפה" "ניהול מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "האוניברסיטה העברית בירושלים" "מדיניות ומינהל בחינוך",
        `education administration programme` "אוניברסיטת תל-אביב" "מינהל ומדיניות בחינוך",
        `education administration programme` "האוניברסיטה הפתוחה" "מינהל, מדיניות, מנהיגות בחינוך",
        `education administration programme` "מכללת אורות ישראל, מכללה אקדמית לחינוך" "ניהול מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "המכללה האקדמית לחינוך אורנים" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "אחווה, המכללה האקדמית לחינוך" "מינהל מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "המכללה האקדמית בית-ברל" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "המכללה האקדמית גורדון בחיפה" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "מכללת ליפשיץ, המכללה האקדמית הדתית לחינוך" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "סמינר הקיבוצים" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "מכללת אוהלו בקצרין" "ארגון וניהול מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "מכללה ירושלים" "ארגון וניהול מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "המרכז ללימודים אקדמיים" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "מכללת סכנין" "ארגון וניהול מערכות חינוך",
        `education administration programme` "מכללת חמדת דרום" "ניהול וארגון מערכות חינוך"

@desc An institution and the name its master's programme in education administration carries there (4.3).
DECLARE `education administration programme` HAS
    `institution of the programme` IS A STRING
    `name of the programme there` IS A STRING

-- 4.3's note: sitting principals of three years and former principals of
-- four of the last ten are exempt from the training certificate.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-3/p22 The heading "הערה"; no rule.

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3/p23 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_1 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is exempt from the training certificate` c IF
        c's `serving principal for 3 consecutive years with 3 approved years and no negative opinion`
    OR  c's `former principal 4 of the last 10 years with 4 approved years and no negative opinion`

@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p23
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the training condition` c IF
    `the training qualifies` (c's `principal training`) OR `is exempt from the training certificate` c

-- ¶32-¶33: the thresholds for principal of a post-primary school (six-,
-- four- or three-year) are set by the Director-General's circular as
-- updated from time to time; the latest (standing order 0203 of March 2019,
-- תשע"ט) sets the four conditions that follow.
@export default Whether a candidate meets the threshold conditions for principal of a post-primary school (upper division) restated in the owners' circular 5779/5
@ref akn:preamble/p32 akn:preamble/p33
GIVEN c IS A `candidate` @desc the candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the threshold conditions` c IF
        `meets the teaching condition` c
    AND `meets the academic condition` c
    AND `meets the pedagogical condition` c
    AND `meets the training condition` c

-- ¶4: one selected before completing the programme must complete it by the
-- programme's end, or the selection is cancelled. Time in months from the
-- selection. "תבוטל בחירתו" is a consequence in the passive, not a duty laid
-- on anyone: the selection is cancelled. The L4 states the consequence as
-- the breach's reason and names no one who cancels, because the text names
-- no one (F-2018-19_tashat_05-c).
@ref akn:art_4/p4
GIVEN `months until the programme ends` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment action`
DECIDE `completing the programme after selection` `months until the programme ends` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `complete the principal training programme`
    WITHIN `months until the programme ends`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "the programme was not completed by its end, so the selection is cancelled (תבוטל בחירתו)"

§§ `הכישורים הרצויים`

-- ¶3: the desirable skills are weighed by the advisers' committee in forming
-- its recommendation; the list, 1-12 in the printed order (the corpus
-- prints the list inside 4.3.2: 1-4 as paragraphs, their numbers at the
-- lines' ends, and 5-12 as its clauses; articles 5-12 until MMS-425).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p12 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p13 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p15 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p17 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p19 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p20 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p21
DECLARE `desirable skill` IS ONE OF
    `knowing the school's particular features`
    `leading, directing and guiding education, teaching and learning`
    `planning a vision and a work plan with the staff`
    `leading a team and teamwork`
    `focusing on the individual, a safe environment, equality`
    `experience teaching pupils with special needs`
    `knowing the law and the Ministry's instructions`
    `positive ties with the community and public bodies`
    `expression in Hebrew and in the school's language`
    `administrative ability: office, accounts and finances`
    `a budgeted pedagogical and organisational plan from data`
    `a school curriculum on the official one`

-- ¶3: each is weighed in the advisers' committee's recommendation; being
-- "desirable", none is a threshold condition.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p3
GIVEN s IS A `desirable skill`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is weighed in the advisers' committee's recommendation` s IF TRUE

GIVEN s IS A `desirable skill`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a threshold condition` s IF FALSE

§§ `הליך הבחירה`

-- akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p22 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p30 Headings ("the selection procedure", "the Ministry representative's role"); no rule.

-- ¶3-¶5: local authorities select by tender under the Interior Ministry's
-- rules (the Local Councils Order 1977, the Municipalities Regulations
-- 1979); every owner of a six-year school must hold a tender for a
-- six-year or independent upper-division principal (joint circular 2.15.7).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p23 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p24 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p24 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p25
GIVEN o IS AN `owner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must select by tender` o IF
    o's `a local authority` OR o's `owns a six-year school`

-- ¶6: the committee includes two Ministry representatives appointed by the
-- district manager, its make-up coordinated with him.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p25
`Ministry representatives on the committee` MEANS 2

-- ¶7-¶8: the owner checks every candidate against the thresholds and
-- prepares a file (the CV and every document proving the thresholds) for
-- each who meets them; before any interview the file is checked in a forum
-- of all the committee's members. The text puts that check in the passive;
-- the owner, on whom ¶7 lays the responsibility for the procedure, is taken
-- to convene it.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p26 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p27
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment action`
DECIDE `checking and filing a candidate` c IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `check the candidate against the thresholds`
    HENCE (IF `meets the threshold conditions` c
           THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                MUST `prepare the candidate file`
                HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                       MUST `have the whole committee check the candidate file before the interview`)
           ELSE FULFILLED)

-- ¶10: section 16(a) of the Supervision Law: no one may employ an education
-- worker, a principal included, without the Director-General's written
-- non-objection.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p29
GIVEN `holds the employment approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment action`
DECIDE `the employment approval` `holds the employment approval` IS
    IF `holds the employment approval`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         SHANT `employ an education worker without the employment approval`

-- ¶13-¶14: the Ministry's representatives join the interviews once the
-- owner has checked the thresholds, and assess each candidate's fitness.
-- ¶15: the committee selects by the owner's rules, but not a candidate the
-- Ministry's representatives found unsuitable. ¶6 and ¶26-¶27: no
-- principal not found fit by the Ministry, nor without its consent.
-- The reading adopted (F-2018-19_tashat_05-b): the positive test governs.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p32 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p33 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p35
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be selected under ¶15` c IF
    `meets the threshold conditions` c AND NOT c's `found unsuitable by a Ministry representative`

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p25 akn:preamble/p26 akn:preamble/p27
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed with the Ministry's consent` c IF
    `meets the threshold conditions` c AND c's `found fit by the Ministry`

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p25 akn:art_4__para_4-3__subpara_2/p35 akn:preamble/p26 akn:preamble/p27
GIVEN c IS A `candidate`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment action`
DECIDE `appointing a principal` c IS
    IF `may be appointed with the Ministry's consent` c AND `may be selected under ¶15` c
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MAY `appoint the candidate as principal`
    ELSE PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         SHANT `appoint the candidate as principal`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and the copies list; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Findings.

-- F-2018-19_tashat_05-a: a deputy principal who managed 10 teachers for
-- five years, with three years' teaching.
`a deputy of a small staff` MEANS `candidate` WITH
    `years of actual teaching in grades 1-12 in Israel` IS 3
    `full school years of actual teaching` IS 3
    `years of proven management` IS 5
    `managed in the education system` IS TRUE
    `team size managed` IS 10
    `recognised master's degree` IS TRUE
    `post-primary pedagogical qualification` IS TRUE
    `principal training` IS `the Avney Rosha programme completed or eligible`
    `serving principal for 3 consecutive years with 3 approved years and no negative opinion` IS FALSE
    `former principal 4 of the last 10 years with 4 approved years and no negative opinion` IS FALSE
    `found unsuitable by a Ministry representative` IS FALSE
    `found fit by the Ministry` IS FALSE

`the thirty-employee test read for both systems` MEANS
    `a deputy of a small staff`'s `team size managed` AT LEAST 30
`the management alternative reads two ways for a small education team` MEANS
    `meets the management alternative` `a deputy of a small staff`
    AND NOT `the thirty-employee test read for both systems`
#ASSERT `the management alternative reads two ways for a small education team`

-- F-2018-19_tashat_05-b: the Ministry's representatives made no finding
-- either way about the same candidate.
`the Ministry tests disagree when the Ministry made no finding` MEANS
        `may be selected under ¶15` `a deputy of a small staff`
    AND NOT `may be appointed with the Ministry's consent` `a deputy of a small staff`
#ASSERT `the Ministry tests disagree when the Ministry made no finding`

-- F-2018-19_tashat_05-c: ¶4's "תבוטל בחירתו" is in the passive; it names
-- no one who cancels the selection.
GIVETH A LIST OF Party
DECIDE `the parties ¶4 names as cancelling the selection` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `¶4 names no one to cancel the selection` IF
    `the parties ¶4 names as cancelling the selection` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `¶4 names no one to cancel the selection`

-- Examples.
`a sitting principal without Avney Rosha` MEANS `candidate` WITH
    `years of actual teaching in grades 1-12 in Israel` IS 12
    `full school years of actual teaching` IS 12
    `years of proven management` IS 4
    `managed in the education system` IS TRUE
    `team size managed` IS 40
    `recognised master's degree` IS TRUE
    `post-primary pedagogical qualification` IS TRUE
    `principal training` IS `a master's in education administration` FALSE
    `serving principal for 3 consecutive years with 3 approved years and no negative opinion` IS TRUE
    `former principal 4 of the last 10 years with 4 approved years and no negative opinion` IS FALSE
    `found unsuitable by a Ministry representative` IS FALSE
    `found fit by the Ministry` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `meets the threshold conditions` `a sitting principal without Avney Rosha`
#ASSERT NOT `the training qualifies` (`a master's in education administration` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `is a threshold condition` `experience teaching pupils with special needs`

#TRACE `completing the programme after selection` 6 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `complete the principal training programme` AT 5
#TRACE `appointing a principal` `a sitting principal without Avney Rosha` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `appoint the candidate as principal` AT 1

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over a finite space of candidates: 0 to 6 years of
-- teaching, 4 or 5 years of management, in education or not, staffs of 10
-- or 30; a degree and a qualification or not; every kind of training; the
-- two exemptions; the Ministry's two findings.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`every training` MEANS
    LIST `the Avney Rosha programme completed or eligible`,
         `the Avney Rosha programme begun in July of the year before the posts are published` TRUE,
         `the Avney Rosha programme begun in July of the year before the posts are published` FALSE,
         `an earlier Ministry programme for principals completed`,
         `the 5769 pilot master's in school leadership`,
         `a master's in education administration` TRUE,
         `a master's in education administration` FALSE,
         `none`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      t IS A `principal training`
      x IS A BOOLEAN
      u IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `candidate`
DECIDE `a checked candidate` y m e n d t x u f IS
    `candidate` WITH
        `years of actual teaching in grades 1-12 in Israel` IS y
        `full school years of actual teaching` IS y
        `years of proven management` IS m
        `managed in the education system` IS e
        `team size managed` IS n
        `recognised master's degree` IS d
        `post-primary pedagogical qualification` IS d
        `principal training` IS t
        `serving principal for 3 consecutive years with 3 approved years and no negative opinion` IS x
        `former principal 4 of the last 10 years with 4 approved years and no negative opinion` IS FALSE
        `found unsuitable by a Ministry representative` IS u
        `found fit by the Ministry` IS f

-- Condition 1 and its note over years, management and staffs: five years'
-- teaching meets it alone; below five, exactly three full years with five
-- years' management, in education or over a staff of 30 (finding a's
-- reading); more teaching never loses it.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN y YIELD
                all (GIVEN m YIELD
                        all (GIVEN e YIELD
                                all (GIVEN n YIELD
                                        LET c MEANS `a checked candidate` y m e n TRUE `none` FALSE FALSE FALSE
                                        IN      `meets the teaching condition` c
                                                EQUALS (y AT LEAST 5 OR (y AT LEAST 3 AND m AT LEAST 5 AND (e OR n AT LEAST 30)))
                                            AND ((NOT `meets the teaching condition` c)
                                                 OR `meets the teaching condition` (`a checked candidate` (y PLUS 1) m e n TRUE `none` FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
                                    (LIST 10, 30))
                            `both booleans`)
                    (LIST 4, 5))
            (range 0 6)

-- Condition 4 over every kind of training: Avney Rosha, an earlier
-- programme or the pilot master's always; Avney Rosha begun in July only
-- for a tender closing before it ends; a master's in education
-- administration only if begun by 5771; none never. An exemption meets the
-- condition whatever the training.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                    `meets the training condition` (`a checked candidate` 5 5 TRUE 30 TRUE t TRUE FALSE FALSE)
                AND `meets the training condition` (`a checked candidate` 5 5 TRUE 30 TRUE t FALSE FALSE FALSE)
                    EQUALS (NOT (   t EQUALS `none`
                                 OR t EQUALS `the Avney Rosha programme begun in July of the year before the posts are published` FALSE
                                 OR t EQUALS `a master's in education administration` FALSE)))
            `every training`

-- The thresholds over training, degree and teaching: met exactly where all
-- four conditions are.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                all (GIVEN d YIELD
                        all (GIVEN y YIELD
                                LET c MEANS `a checked candidate` y 5 FALSE 10 d t FALSE FALSE FALSE
                                IN  `meets the threshold conditions` c
                                    EQUALS (    `meets the teaching condition` c AND `meets the academic condition` c
                                            AND `meets the pedagogical condition` c AND `meets the training condition` c))
                            (LIST 2, 3, 5))
                    `both booleans`)
            `every training`

-- ¶15 and the Ministry's consent over its two findings, for a qualified
-- candidate: ¶15 bars exactly one found unsuitable; consent asks a finding
-- of fitness; the two part exactly where the Ministry found neither
-- (finding b), and an unqualified candidate passes neither.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN u YIELD
                all (GIVEN f YIELD
                        LET c MEANS `a checked candidate` 5 5 TRUE 30 TRUE `none` TRUE u f
                            q MEANS `a checked candidate` 2 5 TRUE 30 TRUE `none` TRUE u f
                        IN      `may be selected under ¶15` c EQUALS (NOT u)
                            AND `may be appointed with the Ministry's consent` c EQUALS f
                            AND (`may be selected under ¶15` c AND NOT `may be appointed with the Ministry's consent` c) EQUALS ((NOT u) AND (NOT f))
                            AND (NOT `may be selected under ¶15` q)
                            AND (NOT `may be appointed with the Ministry's consent` q))
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- ¶3-¶5 over every owner: a tender exactly for a local authority or the
-- owner of a six-year school.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD
                all (GIVEN s YIELD
                        `must select by tender` (`owner` WITH
                                                    `owns an upper division (10-12 or 9-12)` IS TRUE
                                                    `supervised and budgeted by the Ministry` IS TRUE
                                                    `licensed under the Supervision of Schools Law` IS TRUE
                                                    `a local authority` IS a
                                                    `owns a six-year school` IS s)
                        EQUALS (a OR s))
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- The desirable skills: twelve, all weighed, none a threshold.
`every desirable skill` MEANS
    LIST `knowing the school's particular features`, `leading, directing and guiding education, teaching and learning`,
         `planning a vision and a work plan with the staff`, `leading a team and teamwork`,
         `focusing on the individual, a safe environment, equality`, `experience teaching pupils with special needs`,
         `knowing the law and the Ministry's instructions`, `positive ties with the community and public bodies`,
         `expression in Hebrew and in the school's language`, `administrative ability: office, accounts and finances`,
         `a budgeted pedagogical and organisational plan from data`, `a school curriculum on the official one`
#ASSERT count `every desirable skill` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD `is weighed in the advisers' committee's recommendation` s AND NOT `is a threshold condition` s) `every desirable skill`
